add_claim("Free-kick rule: pick TWO dedicated takers, one left-footed and one right-footed, and stick to them because technique becomes consistent.", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-two-takers", [e_sp])
add_claim("Every player has DIFFERENT free-kick settings - Ronaldo and Messi take them differently and the same technique will not work for both, with curl varying by player (Alexander-Arnold 'curves A LOT', Modric way less).", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-per-player", [e_sp])
add_claim("Use AT LEAST 70% power on free kicks, because anything below that is not guaranteed to clear the wall; THE WALL is the reference for learning how much your taker curls - watch which player in the wall the arrow points at.", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-power-floor", [e_sp])
add_claim("Free-kick aiming: go over the SHORTEST player in the wall and target the TOP corners rather than the centre, using a diagonal swipe rather than a straight one.", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-aiming", [e_sp])
add_claim("Free-kick distance bands: 18-22 yards = curl shot with the inside foot; 23-28 yards = power shot or curled top-corner; 30+ yards = long-shot technique or pass.", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-distance-bands", [e_sp])
add_claim("LIVE-MODE FREE-KICK TIMING TRICK: an opponent can manually move a player onto the goal line and head your free kick away, so wait for them to step onto the line, then SWITCH THE TAKER (which resets where their player is) and shoot immediately.", 2, "setpieces/free-kick-switch-taker-trick", [e_sp], notes="High-value tactical detail")
add_claim("If direct free kicks are unreliable, do not take them: pass to a player near the wall with C and shoot the resulting long shot, or cross into the box.", 3, "setpieces/free-kick-short-pass-alternative", [e_sp])
add_claim("Penalty conversion is reported at 85-90% in Dream League Live and 70-80% in shootouts, and multiple players describe shootout penalties as rigged with predictable run-ups.", 3, "setpieces/penalty-conversion", [e_sp])
add_claim("Penalty techniques: slightly left or right of the middle with moderate power; low C press on either side with a medium A; a light A tap or full-power B to the bottom corners; against the AI, the middle with a slightly powered A (just enough to reach the keeper's head); or aiming one-third away from the keeper toward the post with the pass button held to half or two-thirds power.", 3, "setpieces/penalty-techniques", [e_sp])
add_claim("Penalty execution rule: make the button taps as GENTLE AND QUICK AS POSSIBLE, because holding a split-second too long produces a wild, overpowered shot; always aim for the top or bottom corners.", 2, "setpieces/penalty-tap-gentle", [e_sp])

